<p>Booking a tempo traveller should be simple, yet many group trips go wrong because of small things nobody checked: a tired driver, AC that barely works, or a surprise “permit charge” halfway to the hills. Before you confirm your <strong>tempo traveller booking in Delhi</strong>, run through this 15-point checklist. It takes ten minutes and can save your whole trip.</p>

<h2 id="vehicle">Checks on the vehicle</h2>
<h3>1. Yellow number plate (commercial registration)</h3>
<p>Paid passenger vehicles must be commercially registered and carry a yellow plate. Private white-plate vehicles used commercially can leave you without valid insurance cover.</p>
<h3>2. Valid permit for your route</h3>
<p>Travelling to Uttarakhand, Himachal, Rajasthan or Punjab? The tempo needs a valid tourist permit and must pay the state entry tax. Ask whether the permit cost is included in your quote.</p>
<h3>3. Insurance, fitness and PUC</h3>
<p>Ask the operator to confirm the vehicle’s insurance, fitness certificate and pollution (PUC) certificate are current. A genuine operator will share copies without hesitation.</p>
<h3>4. Model and age of the vehicle</h3>
<p>Newer tempo travellers have better suspension, stronger AC and fewer breakdowns. Ask for the model year and recent photos of the exact vehicle, not stock images.</p>
<h3>5. AC performance</h3>
<p>In a Delhi summer, a weak AC makes a 6-hour drive miserable. Ask about AC vents for every row and, if possible, check the cooling at pick-up before you set off.</p>
<h3>6. Seats, legroom and cleanliness</h3>
<p>Pushback seats, clean covers and curtains make a big difference on long drives. If comfort is a priority, compare a standard tempo with a <a href="maharaja-tempo-traveller-on-rent-in-delhi.php">Maharaja tempo traveller</a>.</p>
<h3>7. Luggage space and roof carrier</h3>
<p>Count your bags. For long hill trips, ask whether a roof carrier with a waterproof cover is available. Our <a href="12-16-20-seater-tempo-traveller-which-to-choose.php">seater comparison guide</a> explains luggage space by size.</p>
<h3>8. Safety equipment</h3>
<p>Check for working seat belts, a first-aid kit, a fire extinguisher and a spare tyre. For children, carry your own child seat.</p>

<h2 id="driver">Checks on the driver</h2>
<h3>9. Experience on your route</h3>
<p>Mountain roads to <a href="delhi-to-manali-tempo-on-rent.php">Manali</a>, Kedarnath or Shimla need a driver with real hill experience. Ask how often they have driven your route.</p>
<h3>10. Rest and driving hours</h3>
<p>A tired driver is the biggest safety risk on long trips. For journeys over 10–12 hours, plan proper breaks or an overnight halt. Avoid schedules that have one driver driving through two nights in a row.</p>
<h3>11. Driver contact before the trip</h3>
<p>You should receive the driver’s name, phone number and vehicle number a day before departure, so you can coordinate pick-ups directly.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">Checks on price and policies</h2>
<h3>12. A written, itemised quote</h3>
<p>Get the per km rate, minimum km per day, driver allowance, toll, parking, permits and night charges in writing. Our <a href="tempo-traveller-on-rent-in-delhi-price-guide.php">tempo traveller price guide</a> explains each item.</p>
<h3>13. How kilometres are counted</h3>
<p>Confirm that kilometres are counted from your pick-up point in Delhi and back (garage-to-garage policies add extra distance). Check whether local sightseeing kilometres are included.</p>
<h3>14. Advance payment and cancellation</h3>
<p>Know how much advance is required, whether it is refundable, and what happens if weather or road closures force a change of plan.</p>
<h3>15. Real reviews and a real office</h3>
<p>Check recent Google reviews and make sure the operator has a working phone number and address. If a price looks too good to be true, extra charges usually appear mid-trip.</p>

<h2 id="red-flags">Red flags to avoid</h2>
<div class="callout warn"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Walk away if you see:</strong> a white private number plate, no written quote, pressure to pay the full amount upfront, refusal to share vehicle photos, or a price far below every other operator in Delhi NCR.</p></div>

